5-12-11T00:17:04Z"},"body":"## Summary\n- Fix tab names not being announced by screen readers in the Godot editor\n- When `_ensure_node()` recreates an AccessKit node, re-apply the stored name so it persists\n\n## Problem\nWhen TabContainer calls `accessibility_update_add_related_controls()`, it triggers `_ensure_node()` which creates a new empty node. TabBar only sets tab properties when `accessibility_item_dirty` is true, so recreated nodes were pushed without names, causing screen readers to announce \"page tab\" without the actual tab name (Scene, Inspector, etc.).\n\n## Solution\nIn `_ensure_node()`, after creating a new node, check if a name was previously stored and re-apply it. This ensures tab names persist across node recreations.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Build with accessibility enabled\n- [x] Open Godot editor with screen reader\n- [x] Navigate to tabs (Scene, Import, FileSystem, etc.)\n- [x] Verify screen reader announces tab names, not just \"page tab\"","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113533/reac